# cmd reads .bat with the console code page and its parser mishandles bare-LF
# line endings (goto, labels and multi-line blocks break).
#
# eol=crlf is NOT enough: it stores LF in the repository and only converts on
# checkout, so a file fetched straight from raw.githubusercontent still arrives
# with bare LFs.  -text marks these as binary-ish, meaning Git stores the exact
# bytes on disk -- CRLF -- and the wire copy is already Windows-ready.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text
*.vbs -text
